{:schema 1
 :date "2026-08-14"
 :receipt/type :diagnosis
 :follows "2026-08-14-external-decomposition-exhausted.edn"

 :finding
 "89% of LDBC IC02 is spent inside `datalog.core/scan*`, and almost all of that is
  `(satisfies? datom.source/IPatternSource db)` -- a protocol check that returns
  false on every call, costing 54x the index read it guards."

 :measured
 {:satisfies-ipatternsource-ns 11305
  :dq-query-one-keyed-pattern-ns 210
  :ratio "54x"
  :host-load 2.92
  :method "200,000 iterations after 3,000 warmup, one JVM"}

 :inside-the-engine
 {:method "temporary phase counters in datalog.core/join-clause, thrown away after the run"
  :ic02-total-ms-per-query 28.905
  :group-by-substitute-ms 0.544 :group-by-pct 1.9
  :scan-ms 25.735 :scan-pct 89.0
  :unify-and-build-ms 1.904 :unify-pct 6.6
  :clause-invocations 180
  :accounted-pct 97.5
  :host-load 3.61}

 :the-arithmetic
 "IC02 issues one `scan*` per distinct substituted pattern: 1 for the first
  clause, 882 for `hasCreator` over the friend set, and about 900 for
  `message/creationDate`. Roughly 1,800 calls at 11.3 microseconds is 20 ms,
  against 25.7 ms measured in `scan*`. The protocol check explains the phase."

 :why-external-probing-could-not-find-it
 "Every arm in the four preceding receipts read the index through
  `arrangement.query/query` or through `:pos`/`:spo` directly. Neither goes
  through `scan*`, so none of them paid the check. The residue was 10x and
  invisible from outside for the same reason: it is not in the data path, it is
  in the dispatch in front of it."

 :three-refuted-hypotheses-in-hindsight
 "Binding representation, generality, the read path -- each was measured and each
  was small. They were all guesses about what the engine DOES with a row. The
  cost was in a decision the engine re-makes before every scan, about what kind
  of thing its database is. Nothing about the shape of the data or the join could
  have suggested that."

 :not-yet-fixed
 "The obvious repair -- decide once per query instead of once per pattern -- is
  not made here. `satisfies?` result depends on the db's type, so caching by
  class is tempting and is wrong in the presence of a later `extend`; threading a
  boolean from the query entry point is correct and touches every `scan*` call
  site. That is a change to make carefully with the suite green, not at the end
  of a measurement."

 :caveats
 ["The phase counters force `scan*`'s result into a vector to time it, which
   changes allocation slightly. The 89% is therefore approximate; the 11.3
   microsecond figure is not, and is measured independently."
  "One query shape. IC09 and IC08 issue far more and far fewer scans respectively,
   so the share will differ; the per-call cost will not."
  "Measured on a materialized-map db, which is what does NOT satisfy the protocol.
   A real IPatternSource would take the other branch and pay a different cost."]}
